v class=\"message\">The Online Convention said that LET THE STREETS RUN RED's layout MAY be finished now.<br /> <br /> Wee!<br /> <br /> Now it's onto proofing!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I said it's in the final stages of layout. I get that you're excited for this book, and appreciate your continued enthusiasm, but please go by what the Monday meeting notes say rather than telling people the book is in proofing. It isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T06:55:16-07:00","id":1396670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1363026-v5-let-the-streets-run-red-what-we-know?p=1396637#post1396637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I said it's in the final stages of layout. I get that you're excited for this book, and appreciate your continued enthusiasm, but please go by what the Monday meeting notes say rather than telling people the book is in proofing. It isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am officially never going to make another interpretation on it or another product's status. I clearly suck at it.<br /> <br /> Now I'm just embarrassed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-15-2020, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T10:59:20-07:00","id":1396695,"title":"","content":"I forgive you oh, minister of misinformation. :<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So for those Kindred staked and awaiting judgment of some sort, where's a good place to have them stashed away? I've a vision of a scene like the book/film Coma (1978). I'm thinking maybe those vampires are sold to the Circulatory System to provide blood to elders trying to stave off the beckoning. There's no intent to actually 'free' them or judge them, not until the cycle of Gehenna pasts, if ever.. I could see these weird blood farms, with tubes of blood being infused in the staked Kindred. Maybe the Kindred are aware of it too. They are helpessly aware that they're in turn farmed for their vitae- the rarest of the Blue Velvet's stock for its most exclusive of patrons. Other thoughts or embellishments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T11:49:37-07:00","id":1396703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruthven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1363026-v5-let-the-streets-run-red-what-we-know?p=1396695#post1396695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgive you oh, minister of misinformation. :<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So for those Kindred staked and awaiting judgment of some sort, where's a good place to have them stashed away? I've a vision of a scene like the book/film Coma (1978). I'm thinking maybe those vampires are sold to the Circulatory System to provide blood to elders trying to stave off the beckoning. There's no intent to actually 'free' them or judge them, not until the cycle of Gehenna pasts, if ever.. I could see these weird blood farms, with tubes of blood being infused in the staked Kindred. Maybe the Kindred are aware of it too. They are helpessly aware that they're in turn farmed for their vitae- the rarest of the Blue Velvet's stock for its most exclusive of patrons. Other thoughts or embellishments?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably have like a bank vault built into an old style John Wick-esque hotel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T20:52:32-07:00","id":1397442,"title":"","content":"A John Wick style hotel might garner too much mortal attention. In reviewing CbN, the closed down Joliet Corrections Center struck a chord, but I'm saving that for something else. I wanted something with a horrid history, that would allow for other supernatural encounters as well, and might explain why it's not &quot;heavily guarded&quot; since the reputation alone is enough to keep mortals and most Kindred away.I'm thinking an abandoned building of what was once the Manteno State Psychiatric Hospital, about 50 miles from Chicago; little more than an hour's drive. This place has an awful, and terrifying real world history. For the sake of the World of Darkness, in consideration of its past horrors, I imagine it might have required a morgue too-- and there our staked Kindred rest. This place is rife with spectres- that alone is enough for mortals to give the place a wide berth. I imagine, nearby there might be a few ghouls or Dominated mortals, who make the rounds, probably police of the town. Here, the torpid forms of Dickie, Victoria Longwood and maybe Lorraine Matthews lay. Can you think of any other Kindred mentioned as staked and disappeared in CbN and the Folios? Maybe, Let the Streets Run Red will give us insight into Lorraine's fate, otherwise, if Jackson did stake her--well, this is a suitably nightmarish location for her torpid form.<br /> <br /> Maybe recently, a wight took residence? A Malkavian wight at that. Damien and the hounds haven't been there in sometime since the decree is to extinguish and not stake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","user":"Ruthven","date":".  Additional thought 06-18-2020, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T20:54:22-07:00","id":1397443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruthven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1363026-v5-let-the-streets-run-red-what-we-know?p=1397442#post1397442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A John Wick style hotel might garner too much mortal attention. In reviewing CbN, the closed down Joliet Corrections Center struck a chord, but I'm saving that for something else. I wanted something with a horrid history, that would allow for other supernatural encounters as well, and might explain why it's not &quot;heavily guarded&quot; since the reputation alone is enough to keep mortals and most Kindred away.I'm thinking an abandoned building of what was once the Manteno State Psychiatric Hospital, about 50 miles from Chicago; little more than an hour's drive. This place has an awful, and terrifying real world history. For the sake of the World of Darkness, in consideration of its past horrors, I imagine it might have required a morgue too-- and there our staked Kindred rest. This place is rife with spectres- that alone is enough for mortals to give the place a wide berth. I imagine, nearby there might be a few ghouls or Dominated mortals, who make the rounds, probably police of the town. Here, the torpid forms of Dickie, Victoria Longwood and maybe Lorraine Matthews lay. Can you think of any other Kindred mentioned as staked and disappeared in CbN and the Folios? Maybe, Let the Streets Run Red will give us insight into Lorraine's fate, otherwise, if Jackson did stake her--well, this is a suitably nightmarish location for her torpid form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please post this in our Chicago Folio's Where I read! I We've several additional adventure hooks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388414-v5-wir-the-chicago-folios-and-let-the-streets-run-red\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/f