om/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-25-2020, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T06:17:10-07:00","id":1415810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1363026-v5-let-the-streets-run-red-what-we-know?p=1415386#post1415386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Walter Nash is a little like Starscream, in that he's a conniving prick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I..Does it mean there'll be a Megatron-like character? Because that would help me create new Chronicle in an instant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Constantinople was <b>not</b> a mistake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26438-thedreamapologist","name":"TheDreamApologist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T06:37:40-07:00","id":1415815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1363026-v5-let-the-streets-run-red-what-we-know?p=1415412#post1415412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, your Ballard is like 1000% more likable than previous versions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The write up was good, but I have to admit I liked him best when he was Baron Harkonnen without the anti-gravity belt to let him float about. Basically, not just evil but vile.<br /> <br /> Edit: On the other hand maybe he could be followed around by his Tremere employee Peter deVires using Movement of the Mind to levitate the Baron Ballard, for a level of surreal ugliness and comedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 09-28-2020, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T08:49:06-07:00","id":1415830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1363026-v5-let-the-streets-run-red-what-we-know?p=1415815#post1415815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The write up was good, but I have to admit I liked him best when he was Baron Harkonnen without the anti-gravity belt to let him float about. Basically, not just evil but vile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I was initially skeptical of making Ballard less of a Complete Monster (see TV tropes) who fed on his family's children and embodied Humanity 1. However, I think that limited his usefulness as almost all player characters in my groups treated him a bit like Jacob Schumpeter in that the only thing to do with Horatio was off him.<br /> <br /> Given he's apparently the most successful Ventrue businessman in the United States (it's kind of funny how few financial wizards ther are among the Clan of Kings we've seen despite seeing New York, Chicago, Washington D.C., and L.A.), it feels sort of like a waste. Plus, he's very plugged into the city's politics that wouldn't have been very well done if he didn't have a humanity of at least 4.<br /> <br /> I also felt that his original Humanity score just made him the &quot;designated bad guy&quot; in his conflict with Capone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: On the other hand maybe he could be followed around by his Tremere employee Peter deVires using Movement of the Mind to levitate the Baron Ballard, for a level of surreal ugliness and comedy. </div> </div> </div>I weirdly had a childe of Kevin Jackson based on &quot;Big Smoke&quot; from Grand Theft Auto III: San Andreas who was obsessed with Dune and Baron Harkonnen. He would use metaphors from the novels &quot;Whoever controls the crack controls the universe.&quot;, &quot;The crack must flow.&quot; The character being on the outs with his sire because while KJ was trying to be more respectable [this was before V5 when he achieved it], Smoke only cared about increasing their drug profits from as many destroyed lives as possible.<br /> <br /> Just a weird personal anecdote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-28-2020, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T19:50:16-07:00","id":1415926,"title":"","content":"Oh wow,<br /> <br /> I am tremendously excited about this weeks' MONDAY NOTES because it announced &quot;They Came From Camp Murder Lake&quot; and I am a HUGE fan of 80s Slashers. How big of a fan am I? I'm probably a bigger fan of slashers than I am of vampires.<br /> <br /> I even wrote a book homaging them.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/books/1590680855l/53573333._SY475_.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'm also a huge fan of HACK/SLASH, have a vast collection of the original classics, Behind the Mask: The Rise of Leslie Vernon, and the amazing parody CAMP GHOUL MOUNTAIN PART IV.<br /> <br /> I'm already full of exciting questions about this volume and want to know if it's going to have it's own Kickstarter. As much as I like Chuck Wendig's work on SLASHERS, I never felt he managed to get quite the inherent cheese and fun that slashers require. I don't think that will be a problem with a variant of THEY CAME FROM BENEATH THE GRAVE.<br /> <br /> This is amazing!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/O52jAYa4Pm8\" data-code=\"O52jAYa4Pm8\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/O52jAYa4Pm8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Oh, right, news about LET THE STREETS RUN RED.<br /> <br /> New art!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Araya-LTSRR.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Very nice.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this is the cover.<br /> <br /> As for news?<br /> <br /> <b>* V5 Let the Streets Run Red \u2013 At WW for approval.</b><br /> <br /> I'm hesitant to make any statements about being in the final stretch but if we are, I'm still as excited about it as I was when the Kickstarter initially announced it. Looking forward to it when it finally does arrive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-28-2020, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T03:33:29-07:00","id":1415957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1363026-v5-let-the-streets-run-red-what-we-know?p=1415926#post1415926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if this is the cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is then it would become my favorite ever! The usage of red gives me both Kill Bill animated sequence vibes, and miasma. The artist made amazing work for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Constantinople was <b>not</b> a mistake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26438-thedreamapologist","name":"TheDreamApologist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"th