t--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Power <b>Prey</b>, Goddamnit. Do you think we worked that wordplay in for nothing?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gasp!<br /> <br /> What have I done!?<br /> <br /> Thanks for the correction. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T20:39:13-07:00","id":1420923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheDreamApologist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1363026-v5-let-the-streets-run-red-what-we-know?p=1420813#post1420813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> GLHF CTPhipps, hoping to see some write-ups <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, setting up the premise has taken some quick thinking as they start in Tampa, Florida and have to move up to the Midwest.<br /> <br /> My current plans is:<br /> <br /> * The player characters enemies in the Anarchs and Camarilla all come together and they're forced out of the city. Also, while the treaty with the local Mokole breaks down. I'm going to have a bunch of various plots come together at once. So it'll feel like a suitable climax.<br /> <br /> * The player characters have already said they're going to call in a favor with the Justicar that dates back from THE FALL OF LONDON campaign and they will be given protection--by giving them Praxis over Gary, Indiana. Which is both a magnificent gift and a backhanded insult.<br /> <br /> * Modius and Juggler will have already disappeared by this time and I'll have Evelyn currently underground with her gang. As such, the PCs will have a chance to set themselves up as rulers of the city a bit before Power Prey begins.<br /> <br /> * I'm going to emphasize Redwood's psychosis and technology (giving him access to drones and maybe able to hack cellphones). I'm also going to use the villain of NIGHTBREED as a visual reference for his video portion.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.du-hd.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Dr.-Decker-Figure.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> * This will help set up the subsequent RUSTED JUNGLE adventure as well as also making friends with Dexker. I'll give a reason for them to go to Willterton related to their Praxis as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T21:03:53-07:00","id":1421098,"title":"","content":"TIL If you have the backer link to the PDF, you can review a title before it becomes viewable to the public. Anyone know if it'll stick or if I should save a copy of the review to google docs for the official release?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T21:27:58-07:00","id":1421106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zahana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1363026-v5-let-the-streets-run-red-what-we-know?p=1421098#post1421098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TIL If you have the backer link to the PDF, you can review a title before it becomes viewable to the public. Anyone know if it'll stick or if I should save a copy of the review to google docs for the official release?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, both myself and STRANGE ASSEMBLY have already posted our reviews of the book.<br /> <br /> Both were nice enough to be included in the Monday Meeting Notes.<br /> <br /> This is just me but I think it will help build buzz for the release in a few weeks (as implied by a recent Onyx Path news video).<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd love to see your review!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T21:47:12-07:00","id":1421108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1363026-v5-let-the-streets-run-red-what-we-know?p=1421106#post1421106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Personally, I'd love to see your review!</div> </div> </div> </div>Luckily I still have that Google Doc open. <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Let the Streets Run Red is a collection of stories for Vampire: the Masquerade 5th Edition (V5). Each story presents a unique tale to tell at your table and unlike many prior campaign books or supplements provides options for how to run each one from either the Camarilla or Anarch point of view. Storyteller Player Characters are given full character treatment so that they don\u2019t end up feeling one-dimensional and there\u2019s enough material to continue using the setting telling many stories of your own.</span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The book contains several new Lore Sheets for V5. There\u2019s a good mix of them that are tied directly to the characters or locations within the stories and others that have a loose affiliation or no connection at all that can work in any setting your game is occurring in. </span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Included are several pre-generated characters that can be used for groups new to the game, existing games that want to take a break and try something different, or just more ready-made SPCs for the Storyteller to use.</span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The four stories present a variety of different challenges for the players to face.</span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Power Prey - The focus in this story is what lengths will the characters go to in order to protect their touchstones.</span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Dying Fields - This story takes the characters out of the city and brings them to a town with more corn than people. </span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Innocence in Blood - Honestly I wish this story didn\u2019t suffer at the constraints of page space. There\u2019s a lot more that Milwaukee and Indianapolis have to offer and this story could have been the foundations of its own supplement.</span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rusted Jungle - For anyone who knows the history that Vampire the Embraced has with Gary Indiana, this story will feel like an old friend. For those who don\u2019t, it still is a fun story.</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T21:48:42-07:00","id":1421109,"title":"","content":"Random Bit:<br /> <br /> Of all things, Parovich becoming a wight has become one of the major bits of my set up for Power Prey. We did the first session this night and I alluded to the Nosferatu Primogen having been killing random people throughout the slums of Gary (where he was moved--for reasons I'll think of later). So the players have to deal with the blackmail and a muthersucking ELDER WIGHT also feeding in their territory.<br /> <br /> Makes things a bit more frantic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T21:49:34-07:00","id":1421110,"title":"","content":"Excellent review, @Zahana!<br /> <br /> It would make me want to buy it.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T17:44:55-08:00","id":1421532,"title":"","content":"MONDAY MEETING NOTES indicate the POD proofs have been ordered. Yay! One step closer to physical copies!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/from-halloween-to-election-eve-spooky-monday-meeting-notes/?fbclid=IwAR2-9ZemPBekTGbDjgw2xqxwrNULXeGPtyZFMfq4GDe2tjCZ3ODaX8BS1cU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/from-halloween-to-election-eve-spooky-monday-meeting-notes/?fbclid=IwAR2-9ZemPBekTGbDjgw2xqxwrNULXeGPtyZFMfq4GDe2tjCZ3ODaX8BS1cU\" target=\"_blank\"> From Halloween to Election Eve: Spooky! [Monday Meeting Notes] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/from-halloween-to-election-eve-spooky-monday-meeting-notes/?fbclid=IwAR2-9ZemPBekTGbDjgw2xqxwrNULXeGPtyZFMfq4GDe2tjCZ3ODaX8BS1cU\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/from-halloween-to-election-eve-spooky-monday-meeting-notes/?fbclid=IwAR2-9ZemPBekTGbDjgw2xqxwrNULXeGPtyZFMfq4GDe2tjCZ3ODaX8BS1cU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, some awesome art.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/KMJ_LTSRR3.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I like this new version of Nosferatu disfigurement -- SLUAGH LOOK!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/KSJ_LTSRR2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> My favorite art from the book. She looks a lot like Oracle from Birds of Prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T00:04:23-08:00","id":1421944,"title":"","content":"So I have my campaign set up for LET THE STREETS RUN RED. It's a bit more action and conspiracy heavy than the main game versus gritty because the players like their Underworld and Blade interpretations but whatcha gonna do. It does link the four adventures well, though. Gaming is so far going swimmingly with Power Prey.<br /> <br /> <b>Running Let the Streets Run Red as one enormous Chronicle</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 1. The player characters got themselves &quot;exiled&quot;/&quot;rewarded&quot; with the city of Gary, Indiana by the Ventrue Justicar, Lucinde, as their reward for helping with the FALL OF LONDON and needing a place that they could stay after being driven from their old city. Modius and Juggler have both vanished so the city is seemingly uninhabited except for Walter Nash as well as a few other Kindred coteries like Evelyn Stephens.<br /> <br /> 2. Power Prey has them dealing with Redwood's blackmail and the Night's Cross but I'm also adding the additional complication of a wight version of <b>Lucien</b>. The 2000 year old Gangrel having been driven insane. The player characters find out that he was captured by the Second Inquisition, tortured, and expermented on so taking him down is a top priority while they deal with all of the craziness.<br /> <br /> 3. When they send Lucian to the Final Death, they'll find that he had some advanced scientific equipment that he shouldn't have like implanted in his body with bio-thaumaturgical experimentation. This is to confuse the PCs and make them wonder if its Technocrats or Tremere or something else. Basically, heighten their paranoia. I was inspired by<b> Night Road </b>and its technomagic Tremere as well as their freakish experiments on vampires.<br /> <br /> 4. Unbeknownst to the players, the Night's Cross is actually the creation of <b>Maxwell</b> who used all of his connections and wealth to outfit a dangerous vampire-hunting paramilitary organization for the purpose of exterminating his enemies before he will rush into sweep up the group after he's caused enough chaos. A classic false flag operation. Eric Sharpe in this game will be an Embraced Inquisitor that Maxwell has bent.<br /> <br /> 5. The super-tech and experimentation is due to Maxwell having an ally in <b>Doctor Mortius</b> (DUM DUM) from <i>Milwaukee by Night</i> and the <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i>. He's been conducting experiments on how to control the Beckoning, Wightdom, and other things. He's agreed to support Maxwell as Prince of Chicago if he's funded to all his activities. It was with Maxwell's help he set up his Ashfinders cult.<br /> <br /> 6. The players will be following Doctor Mortius' trail when they arrive in Willteron and discover the whole nightmarish Children of the Corn cult there. I'm thinking it will be <b>Nerissa Blackwater</b> that is their goddess and the cult is her Bahari. Doctor Moritus has been merrily working there this entire time. They can confront him there and get some answers. However, they may actually need his help if they need to bind Nerissa back to the Earth. Nerissa in this game would be a 5th Generation Drowned of an Unknown Clan. They can also make an alliance with her and the Lilin if they want.<br /> <br /> Basically, the players can choose to let Cthulhu loose, placate her, or bind her for another hundred years or so. It also makes Doctor Mortius potentially look more awesome as he might have been the one to bind her relatively recently.<br /> <br /> 7. Doctor Mortius will point them to <b>Mark Decker</b> who is Maxwell's primary support in the region and the person who has been unwittingly arming the Second Inquisition. Mark will happily testify against Maxwell with the Justicar and get the former Chicago Prince's final death going if the PCs do him a favor and get his childe back. Mark was using Maxwell and the Night's Cross to destroy the excess Kindred in the region and gather all the hunters in the area for one place where they could be destroyed. He will be pretty open about this &quot;treason&quot; and suggest if the PCs cared about their fellow vampires that they were being naive.<br /> <br /> I may also spruce up Indianapolis somehow but not sure how yet.<br /> <br /> 8. The PCs going against Decker in his adventure is very likely but they should want to go against the Followers of Set too and maybe ally with the Anarchs in Gary against everyone. The &quot;good&quot; option is to give Honor over to Anita Wainwright or Evelyn Stephens. Even then it's an unstable alliance.<br /> <br /> 9. <i>Rusted Jungle</i> will end the chronicle with Maxwell launching his attacks against Chicago, blaming the Second Inquisition and also the Anarchs for &quot;taking advantage of the situation.&quot;<br /> <br /> They can side with:<br /> <br /> * Maxwell who will be okay with them having eliminated so many of his assets because that's the price of doing business. As Prince of Chicago, he'll make them his Primogen and plan to use the Night Cross to spread his reach even further.<br /> * The Camarilla who declare Maxwell part of the Red List (in which case he's going to declare himself &quot;Baron&quot; of Chicago but is doomed no matter what--the issue is how many Kindred he takes down with him rather than whether he'll go down)<br /> * The Anarchs who will emerge as a real power in the city but potentially resent the PCs being the local Praxis.<br /> * I'll also add a 4th option with siding with <b>Sullivan Dane</b> who has realized the potential of the Night's Cross and the some 100+ American soldiers that Maxwell has trained, brainwashed, and equipped. Sullivan plans to free them and use them as weapons against evil, starting with Maxwell, and potentially allied with the PCs.<br /> <br /> They might end up with Milwaukee, Chicago, and Gary all combining into one huge super-state for Kindred in the region.<br /> <br /> Whew!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That should be a six month long Chronicle if I'm lucky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a hre